// Exercise 3.3 - fill the shape, twice.
//
// The template from 3.2 is given below, so this file stands on its own. Your job is the
// two justifications under it.
//
// Write `graceful` first: the same argument as 3.1, but with the conclusion and the
// confronting strategy now coming from the template instead of being written again. Then
// write `accurate` - accuracy against the 80% bar. The second one is where the template
// earns itself: you will find there is very little left to write.
//
// Fill a hook by naming it, scoped to the template:  quality_gate:measured
//
// One hook is not like the other. The measurement needs a sub-argument under it - a
// number nobody produced proves nothing. The bar is agreed elsewhere and merely cited,
// so a single piece of evidence is enough. A hook is a slot, not a fixed size.
//
// Check your work with:   the notepad icon in the preview panel, or
//                         jpipe diagnostic -i 03_implements.jd
// Crib the syntax from:   ../../chapter_2/template.jd

template quality_gate {

    conclusion holds    is "The quality bar is met"
    strategy   confront is "Confront the measurement with the bar"

    @support measured is "The metric has been measured"
    @support bar      is "The bar is agreed"

    confront supports holds
    measured supports confront
    bar      supports confront

}

justification graceful implements quality_gate {

    // The first hook is filled for you, to show what naming one looks like.
    sub-conclusion quality_gate:measured is "The severe-error rate has been measured"

    // TODO the sub-argument under it: the strategy and the evidence you wrote in 3.1,
    //      and the supports links joining them to quality_gate:measured.

    // TODO fill quality_gate:bar with a single piece of evidence: where does the 5%
    //      come from?

}

